## Editor.cpp/Editor::command
a file -> sent ["ide: param set editor file <here>/main/Main.cpp"]; started []; answered ["opened <here>/main/Main.cpp in the editor"]
a folder -> sent ["ide: param set graph folder <here>/sub"]; started []; answered ["opened <here>/sub in the graph"]
a path that names nothing -> throws runtime_error: "<here>/Gone.h names nothing, as a typed path counts from the folder the prompt shows"
a path that names nothing, its name held elsewhere -> throws runtime_error: "<here>/main/Twice.h names nothing, as a typed path counts from the folder the prompt shows; the view holds <here>/one/Twice.h"
a path through .. -> sent ["ide: param set editor file <here>/sub/../view.vlp"]; started []; answered ["opened <here>/sub/../view.vlp in the editor"]
a word the view holds not -> throws runtime_error: "the view holds no file named Gone.h; a path names any, as ./Gone.h in the folder the prompt shows"
a word the view holds once -> sent ["ide: param set editor file <here>/main/Main.cpp"]; started []; answered ["opened <here>/main/Main.cpp in the editor"]
a word the view holds twice -> throws runtime_error: "the view holds 2 files named Twice.h: <here>/one/Twice.h, <here>/two/Twice.h; a path names one"
an image, its ending in capitals -> sent ["ide: param set viewer file <here>/pic.PNG"]; started []; answered ["opened <here>/pic.PNG as a preview"]
none -> sent ["ide: param set editor file <here>/view.vlp"]; started []; answered ["opened <here>/view.vlp in the editor"]

## Editor.cpp/Editor::in_program
a file -> sent []; started ["code <here>/main/Main.cpp"]; answered ["opened <here>/main/Main.cpp with code"]
a folder -> sent []; started ["code <here>/sub"]; answered ["opened <here>/sub with code"]
code not on the PATH -> throws runtime_error: "code is not on the PATH; `: param set edit program <name>` names another"
none -> sent []; started ["code <here>"]; answered ["opened <here> with code"]
the window alone running, a folder -> throws runtime_error: "<here>/sub: cannot be read; the editor in the window opens files, and `: param unset edit window` sends each to code"
the window alone running, an image -> sent ["ide: param set editor file <here>/pic.PNG"]; started []; answered ["opened <here>/pic.PNG in the editor"]

## Editor.cpp/image
.png -> false
a -> false
a.JPG -> true
a.PNG -> true
a.jpeg -> true
a.png -> true
a.png/b -> false
a.webp -> false

## Editor.cpp/named, folder
/ -> named true, folder true
